    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1323">

                <pb facs="0894" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/93.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Davis.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A. A. Neil and J. L. Burt, American citizens, owning bakery Guadalajara, known as
                    “Cía Galletera Nacional “report that Constitutionalist authorities have imposed
                    forced loan five thousand pesos, and these Americans desire postponement time
                    limit to pay until they can reach Guadalajara by steamer sailing California for
                    Manzanillo September 26.</p>
                <p>Endeavor to secure desired postponement, and in reporting result of your efforts,
                    state briefly facts regarding nature of loan imposed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
